Subject: clc_helpers: use getTargetOpts() for Clang 21 compatibility

Clang 21 made CompilerInvocationBase::TargetOpts protected and changed
it from `TargetOptions` to `std::shared_ptr<TargetOptions>`. Direct
field access no longer compiles. The public accessor `getTargetOpts()`
returns a `TargetOptions&` which is what `TargetInfo::CreateTargetInfo`
expects.

Builds against both Clang 20 (where the field was public and a value)
and Clang 21 (where it's protected and a shared_ptr).

This matches the upstream Mesa fix that landed in 25.2+.

--- a/src/compiler/clc/clc_helpers.cpp
+++ b/src/compiler/clc/clc_helpers.cpp
@@ -874,7 +874,7 @@ clc_compile_to_llvm_module(LLVMContext &llvm_ctx,
                            diag_opts));

    c->setTarget(clang::TargetInfo::CreateTargetInfo(
-                   c->getDiagnostics(), c->getInvocation().TargetOpts));
+                   c->getDiagnostics(), c->getInvocation().getTargetOpts()));

    c->getFrontendOpts().ProgramAction = clang::frontend::EmitLLVMOnly;

